# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon — on CI, to a remote builder —
# and its inputs are recorded in provenance attestations. Treat everything in it
# as published: no credential, token, private key, or local state belongs here.
#
# This file must stay at least as strict as .gitignore. The Dockerfile COPYs only
# Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, src/, and policy.example.json; everything excluded
# below is either bulk that would only bloat the context or material that must
# never reach a build machine.
#
# Do NOT blanket-ignore *.json: policy.example.json is COPY'd into the image.

# --- Build output, VCS metadata, and local tooling -------------------------
target/
.git/
.gitmodules
.github/
.tokensave/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.playwright-mcp/
site/public/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# --- Local databases and journals ------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal

# --- Documentation (never COPY'd; README stays for buildx/agent consumers) --
*.md
!README.md
# The Helm chart is a deployment artifact, not a build input.
charts/

# --- Test harness state ----------------------------------------------------
# The navra configs embed token_hash values, and results/ holds recorded runs.
tests/e2e/results/
tests/e2e/policy.generated.json
tests/e2e/*.toml

# --- Credentials, tokens, private keys, and local policy -------------------
# Superset of .gitignore: same entries plus the usual secret-shaped names.
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
service-account*.json
secret*.json
secrets*.json
token*.json
.gws-policy.json
gws-policy.json
.env*
auth/
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
.htpasswd
.netrc
.git-credentials
.npmrc
.pypirc
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
